 "hook": {
  "text": "THESE AREN'T\nDICE.",
  "until": 2.6,
  "y": 0.1,
  "size": 118,
  "accent": [
   "DICE."
  ]
 },
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "These little stone cubes are four thousand years old. They're not dice.",
   "emph": [
    "dice."
   ],
   "caption": "These little stone cubes are 4,000 years old. They're not dice."
  },
  {
   "text": "They're weights. Polished cubes of banded stone, from Harappa and Mohenjo-daro.",
   "emph": [
    "weights."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The smallest weighs less than a gram. The most common, about fourteen grams.",
   "emph": [
    "gram."
   ],
   "caption": "The smallest weighs less than a gram. The most common, about 14 grams."
  },
  {
   "text": "And here's the trick: each one doubles the last. One, two, four, eight, sixteen, thirty-two, sixty-four.",
   "emph": [
    "doubles"
   ],
   "caption": "And here's the trick: each one doubles the last. 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64."
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the big ones jump in tens and hundreds... the way we count today.",
   "emph": [
    "today."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Cities a thousand kilometres apart used the same set.",
   "emph": [
    "same"
   ],
   "caption": "Cities 1,000 kilometres apart used the same set."
  },
  {
   "text": "Even on Bahrain, an island in the Gulf, archaeologists found weights that match theirs.",
   "emph": [
    "match"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "No king we know of. No law we can read. Yet a whole civilisation agreed on the same weights.",
   "emph": [
    "agreed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Who checked them? We don't know.",
   "emph": [
    "know."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And that same obsession with order was built into their cities... homes with their own bathrooms, and drains under the streets.",
   "emph": [
    "drains"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So next time you see a little stone cube... look again at",
   "emph": [
    "again"
   ]
  }
 ],
